  "result": "Subcommands now pick up their defaults from `default_map`. All tests pass (1907 passed, 102 skipped), and the new test fails if the fix is removed.\n\n- **Fix** (`src/click/core.py:392`): a subcommand's context now takes only its own entry from the parent's `default_map` (`parent.default_map.get(info_name)`) instead of the whole map. If there's no entry for that subcommand, it falls back to the option's normal default.\n- **Test** (`test_default_map_subcommand` in `tests/test_defaults.py`) checks four cases:\n  - a direct subcommand;\n  - a nested group (`db init`);\n  - a `default_map` set through `context_settings`;\n  - a missing entry falling back to the option default.\n- **Changelog:** 8.5.0 is already released, so I added a new \"Version 8.5.1 \u2013 Unreleased\" section to `CHANGES.md` for this entry.\n\nNothing is committed yet.",
